'''Proximity Shield''' is a [[receiving damage|defensive]] [[Area of effect|area of effect]] ability used by a monster, taking the form of a dome with the user at its centre. The user and their allies within the shielded area are protected from direct damage from enemies outside the shield. 

==Mechanics==
A Proximity Shield removes the damage of [[hit]]s coming from enemies outside the shield. It does not physically obstruct objects or projectiles like a {{il|Frost Wall}}; it simply checks the locations of the entity that hit and the entity that was hit. Removing all hit damage also prevents effects that require non-zero damage, such as [[ailments]]. Proximity shield does ''not'' prevent hits entirely, nor does it prevent non-ailment [[debuff]]s applied by hits, including [[damage over time]] debuffs such as {{il|Essence Drain}} or {{il|Corrupting Fever}}.

To counter proximity shield monsters, the player can:
* enter the shield
* inflict non-ailment [[damage over time]] 
* apply damaging ailments without a direct hit, e.g. [[proliferation]] 
* make their [[minion]]s or [[proxies]] enter the shield, or create them directly inside it 

Several variations of proximity shield exist:  
* The {{C|normal|[[Temporal Proximity Shield]]}} modifier can occur on enemies randomly. It also inflicts a debuff {{stl|Temporal Bubble}}, that slows [[action speed]], [[cooldown]] recovery rate, and debuff expiration. 
* [[Expedition]]'s Unearthed Soldiers temporarily buff themselves and nearby allies with a directional proximity shield, which can be bypassed by attacking from behind in addition to proximity.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/174993814845521922/175005585203396622/874436849928634388</ref>
* Specific monster types can have proximity shields as a [[skill]]. 

Players can benefit from proximity shields by stealing modifiers from enemies with effects like {{il|Headhunter}}, {{il|Inspired Learning}}, {{il|Behead Support}}, or by spawning allies with proximity shields, for example with {{il|Raise Spectre}} or {{il|Dominating Blow}}. 

